2026-10-28T17:39:30.9216240Z [11] ◆ I triaged issue #26 as a usage question and sent two safe outputs: the `question` label and one comment.
2026-10-28T17:39:30.9216712Z   
2026-10-28T17:39:30.9217959Z   - **Why it's a question:** the reporter is working through a Terraform CLI tutorial (assigning variable values from a file) and doesn't understand an error shown only in a screenshot. The report names no AWS resource and gives no error text, and the duplicate search found nothing close.
2026-10-28T17:39:30.9219698Z   - **Label:** `question`. The form had already added `bug`, and the validator warned that a type label was already set. I added `question` anyway because `bug` doesn't fit a tutorial question. A maintainer may want to remove `bug`.
2026-10-28T17:39:30.9221437Z   - **Comment:** it thanks the author and points them to the community forum at `https://discuss.hashicorp.com/c/terraform-providers/tf-aws`, ending with the standard automated-triage footer. It gives no technical advice.
2026-10-28T17:39:30.9222287Z   
2026-10-28T17:39:30.9222848Z   The validator passed with that one warning. The safe-output calls returned success; I did not check their effect on GitHub.
